# Dependencies
# BOTH patterns are required. Docker matches a bare `node_modules` at the
# CONTEXT ROOT ONLY, so packages/db/node_modules and apps/*/node_modules were
# copied into the image — on Windows complete with symlinks pointing at
# C:/Users/... , which resolve to nothing on Linux. They then clobbered the
# links pnpm had just built inside the container, and tsc lost @prisma/client
# entirely: 130 errors, every one downstream of two unresolvable imports.
#
# A clean clone builds fine, so this only bites when building from a machine
# that has installed dependencies — which is every developer's.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build outputs
.next
dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Env & secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*

# Git & IDE
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Large attachments & docs not needed for build
attached_assets
docs
artifacts
*.md

# Testing
e2e
playwright.config.ts
coverage

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.log
